<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <RootNamespace>JoyceCode.Tests</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Joyce\Joyce.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Pre-existing navigation test files were written against an older NavLane /
    Pipe / TemporalConstraint API and have substantial drift (float-vs-int
    parameter mismatches, missing `using System.Linq;`). They have never
    actually been compiled — there was no .csproj here until TALE-SOCIAL D4
    wired one up. Excluded for now; revive when someone updates them against
    the current navigation API.

    The engine/streets folder IS compiled as of WP-0 of the streets generator
    rework. The old StreetGenerationDiagnosticsTests that used to live there was
    deleted rather than revived: it asserted only Assert.True(true), and drove
    generation through ClusterDesc.StrokeStore(), which needs ClusterStorage in
    the I container and would hit the cluster cache. It has been replaced by
    StreetHarness + StreetDeterminismTests, which drive engine.streets.Generator
    directly with no container and no cache.

    The engine/tale/RoutingPreferencesTests.cs file is clean and runs as
    part of the suite (10 passing tests), as do the new TALE-SOCIAL D4
    bake tests in engine/tale/bake/.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="engine\navigation\**\*.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
